{%- comment -%}
  Per-section spacing.

  Sections pick from three tiers rather than setting their own numbers. Uniform
  rhythm is what makes a page read as a list instead of a composition, so the
  tiers sit far apart: major is 1.75x standard, minor is half.

  Parameters:
    id      section id
    top     'major' | 'standard' | 'minor' | 'none'   (default 'standard')
    bottom  as above
    extra   additional declarations scoped to this section
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign tier_top = top | default: 'standard'
  assign tier_bottom = bottom | default: 'standard'

  comment
    The tiers are fixed pixel tokens, which meant `major` was the same gap on a
    1440px desktop and a 390px phone. Two stacked major sections then put some
    266px of empty space between them, over two thirds of a phone screen
    showing nothing at all.

    Each tier is therefore clamped between a floor and a vw share rather than
    used raw. The vw term only wins on narrow viewports, so the desktop rhythm is
    exactly the designed token and the phone gets a proportional share of the
    screen instead of a fixed pixel count. The tokens themselves are left
    alone, so anything reading --space-* directly is unaffected.
  endcomment
  case tier_top
    when 'major'
      assign value_top = 'max(2.75rem, min(var(--space-major), 11vw))'
    when 'minor'
      assign value_top = 'max(1.25rem, min(var(--space-minor), 4vw))'
    when 'none'
      assign value_top = '0px'
    else
      assign value_top = 'max(2rem, min(var(--space-standard), 7vw))'
  endcase

  case tier_bottom
    when 'major'
      assign value_bottom = 'max(2.75rem, min(var(--space-major), 11vw))'
    when 'minor'
      assign value_bottom = 'max(1.25rem, min(var(--space-minor), 4vw))'
    when 'none'
      assign value_bottom = '0px'
    else
      assign value_bottom = 'max(2rem, min(var(--space-standard), 7vw))'
  endcase
-%}
{% style %}
  #shopify-section-{{ id }} {
    --section-padding-block-start: {{ value_top }};
    --section-padding-block-end: {{ value_bottom }};
    {{ extra }}
  }
{% endstyle %}
